{"uid":"78df713ed78ddf89","name":"test_absorption_streak_does_not_force_verify_under_budget_with_corroborated_progress","fullName":"tests.test_progress_budget_task013#test_absorption_streak_does_not_force_verify_under_budget_with_corroborated_progress","historyId":"dc6e523e40744f72dd20147d89fed366","time":{"start":1791969397424,"stop":1791969398659,"duration":1235},"description":"The v0.19 B.2 hand-off (`test_three_consecutive_commit_only_\n    iterations_hand_the_task_to_verify` in `tests/test_worker_hat.py`) used\n    to force ANY 3 consecutive commit-only iterations on one task to\n    `awaiting-validation` -- commits alone were enough, with no notion of\n    a budget at all. Here the SAME three consecutive commit-only\n    iterations each ALSO carry a corroborated `commit` progress claim, and\n    the seeded task's default budget (`estimatedIterations` absent, so\n    `1 + 2 == 3`) covers all three (`used` reaches exactly 3, never past\n    it) -- so `budget_exempt` holds for every one of them, and the\n    hand-off this task retires must never fire: the task stays\n    `in-progress`, and `taskAbsorptionStreak` on `status.json` never\n    accumulates past `{}`.","descriptionHtml":"<p>The v0.19 B.2 hand-off (<code>test_three_consecutive_commit_only_ iterations_hand_the_task_to_verify</code> in <code>tests/test_worker_hat.py</code>) used<br />\nto force ANY 3 consecutive commit-only iterations on one task to<br />\n<code>awaiting-validation</code> -- commits alone were enough, with no notion of<br />\na budget at all. Here the SAME three consecutive commit-only<br />\niterations each ALSO carry a corroborated <code>commit</code> progress claim, and<br />\nthe seeded task's default budget (<code>estimatedIterations</code> absent, so<br />\n<code>1 + 2 == 3</code>) covers all three (<code>used</code> reaches exactly 3, never past<br />\nit) -- so <code>budget_exempt</code> holds for every one of them, and the<br />\nhand-off this task retires must never fire: the ta